  <content>
  <section><title>Lesson Narrative</title>
<para>In an earlier lesson, students used scatter plots to perform linear regression on a data set. In this lesson, students will familiarize themselves with graphing technology in order to display a data set modeling a quadratic function. They will learn how to use this graphing technology to analyze the data set and generate an equation for a curve of best fit. These equations, modeling real-world situations, can be used to make predictions about those situations.</para>
<title>Learning Goals (Teacher Facing)</title>
<list>
  <item> Use graphing technology, such as Desmos, to input a data set modeling a quadratic function and display a scatter plot of the data. </item>
  <item> Generate an quadratic equation for a curve of best, or regression curve, using graphing technology. </item>
  <item> Analyze a situation modeled by a quadratic function and use a curve of best fit to make predictions about that situation. </item>
</list>
<title>Learning Targets (Student Facing)</title>
<list>
  <item> Graph a quadratic data set using technology. </item>
  <item> Find a regression curve, or curve of best fit, using a quadratic data set. </item>
  <item> Use a regression curve to create a quadratic model for making predictions. </item>
  <item> Make predictions about a real-world situation using a quadratic data set. </item>
</list>


